{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion","id":1129520,"title":"Heroic Vampires and Other Setting Hacks? (Setting Hack/Homebrew General Discussion)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-15T18:05:41-07:00","id":1129520,"title":"Heroic Vampires and Other Setting Hacks? (Setting Hack/Homebrew General Discussion)","content":"Okay, I have a question to ask and an idea to share.<br /> <br /> The big question I want to ask in this thread is &quot;What are your setting hacks?&quot; and this can apply to both 1e setting hacks and 2e setting hacks.<br /> <br /> Here is my biggest setting hack, which I apply to 1e Requiem (I don't play 2e, the mechanical and setting changes aren't my cup of tea)<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the possibility of heroic Vampires in the New World of Darkness (and the Classic WoD as well). I mainly play 1e, sans Predator's Taint and the Strix (and the emotional deadness fluff as well) and I like applying setting hacks where Kindred are not emotionally dead nor are they automatically evil. Instead, they have free will to be good or evil, and there are both heroic vampires and villainous vampires, with the majority of Kindred just being ordinary citizen types who just want to live their unlives as peaceably as possible.<br /> <br /> As a general rule, my games have three heroic covenants (Carthians, Ordo Dracul, Circle of the Crone) and three villainous covenants (Invictus, Lancea Sanctum, Belial's Brood) with VII and the Strix excised from the setting completely. But I'm experimenting with other setting hacks as well that will turn 1e Requiem into an anime-influenced Action-Adventure setting instead of the assumed Gothic Personal Horror setting (and there is nothing wrong with either interpretation of WoD/CofD).<br /> <br /> The great thing about nWoD 1e (and CofD 2e), is that the whole franchise was designed to be a toolbox where you could eat the chicken and throw away the bone. There was no metaplot and little if any objective truths to the early nWoD setting. The issue was that some people mistook the default setting assumption of personal horror as the only setting assumption, instead of one out of many equally valid options. The release of Mirrors in 2010 only seems to have confirmed my toolbox theory.<br /> <br /> I love the toolkit approach of New World of Darkness and so I ask the question again.<br /> <br /> What are your setting hacks for Vampire: The Requiem?<br /> <br /> The main purpose of this thread is to discuss our own setting hacks and homebrew material for Requiem, can be both 1e and 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 08-15-2017, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:21:07-07:00","id":1129533,"title":"","content":"How exactly can you portray a parasitic race that play with the notion of abuse and rape every time they feed as heroic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-15-2017, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:23:30-07:00","id":1129535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1129533#post1129533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly can you portray a parasitic race that play with the notion of abuse and rape every time they feed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I downplay or excise those elements. In my games, Kindred can also feed off of animals, willing donors, or not even kill those they feed on. It's like eating meat in my setting, only you don't even have to kill your food source!<br /> <br /> I never was big on &quot;personal horror&quot;. In my opinion, I find personal horror to be boring misery tourism. Now this is only my opinion, based on my own personal experiences, so feel free to disagree with me and take my words with a grain of salt!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:31:59-07:00","id":1129541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1129535#post1129535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I downplay or excise those elements. In my games, Kindred can also feed off of animals, willing donors, or not even kill those they feed on. It's like eating meat in my setting, only you don't even have to kill your food source!<br /> <br /> I never was big on &quot;personal horror&quot;. In my opinion, I find personal horror to be boring misery tourism. Now this is only my opinion, based on my own personal experiences, so feel free to disagree with me and take my words with a grain of salt!</div> </div> </div> </div>At that point, why play a game about vampires at all? You'd have to cut out and modify a heck of a lot less of, say, a superhero game, or anything over in Scion or Trinity. The CofD has always been pretty huge on the personal horror, and it seems like more trouble than it's worth to attempt to rework the thematic heart of these games.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To further explain; I'm not opposed, I'm just curious what's there for you in these games if the foundation rubs you the wrong way. It reminds me a lot of a friend of mine who left these forums, who was insistent on making Promethean not a game about becoming human despite that nearly being the whole of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-15-2017, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:40:50-07:00","id":1129545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1129535#post1129535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I downplay or excise those elements. In my games, Kindred can also feed off of animals, willing donors, or not even kill those they feed on. It's like eating meat in my setting, only you don't even have to kill your food source!<br /> <br /> I never was big on &quot;personal horror&quot;. In my opinion, I find personal horror to be boring misery tourism. Now this is only my opinion, based on my own personal experiences, so feel free to disagree with me and take my words with a grain of salt!</div> </div> </div> </div>Still animal abuse, and if the Kiss is still an element, people becoming addicted to the kiss is still morally reprehensible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:55:01-07:00","id":1129550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1129535#post1129535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never was big on &quot;personal horror&quot;. In my opinion, I find personal horror to be boring misery tourism. Now this is only my opinion, based on my own personal experiences, so feel free to disagree with me and take my words with a grain of salt!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be mean (so my apologies if I come across that way), but if you don't like personal horror, why are you playing ChronDark to begin with? Personal horror is ChronDark's jam, it's gooey center, so if you don't like it, you should probably be playing another game. I mean, play it if you want, I just don't see why you would wanna play it if you don't like the very foundation it's based on is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:57:33-07:00","id":1129554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion#post1129520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have a question to ask and an idea to share. Actually, there's two questions I have to ask.<br /> <br /> First off is the elephant in the living room. Why the hostility to the concept of heroic vampires? I've gotten tired of people throwing around phrases like &quot;Vampions&quot; or &quot;Supers with Fangs&quot; as insults, and I also don't like the idea that personal horror is the only way to play Requiem and that if you're playing anything other than personal horror, you're &quot;playing the game wrong&quot; and should play &quot;Some Other Game&quot;. This attitude was a major problem on the old White Wolf forums, RPG.net, and is still a problem on other discussion sites as well. Onyx Path Forums isn't as bad for it as other places, but the attitude still crops up every once in a while. But that's not the major reason why I posted this thread, it's merely something I need to get out of the way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, first off: there's nothing wrong with playing the game the way you like it. There's nothing wrong with ditching the gothic horror aspects of the game in the name of adventure and action.<br /> <br /> I think the thing that you (and I mean specifically you, but others too) run up against is a problem of context. When many people think of Vampions and Super Heroes with fangs, they think of bad player experiences they've had. &quot;Oh look, here comes Big McLargehuge of Clan Kickass who's also an orphan and answers to no man; he has no backstory, and he has no motivation beyond doing sweet moves and looking awesome. Won't that be a fun addition to my subtle chronicle of intrigue and personal horror.&quot; The problem in that scenario isn't that there's anything inherently wrong with playing a campy <i>Blade </i>expie. It's that many people who've dealt with that character archetype associate it with a negative <i>player </i>stereotype. To many people, that character type indicates the player doesn't want to engage with the story, and would rather play out a power fantasy that the rest of the table doesn't want any part of.<br /> <br /> But it's more complicated than that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Danse Macabre, p. 178</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s lots of reasons a player might chose to create the isolated and unconnected badass, and unfortunately many of them relate to bad play experiences in which a Storyteller or other players abused his sense of fun by using those connections to make him feel inadequate about his character, vulnerable, or ineffective.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The core of the problem is miscommunication (and also that people are often jerks, but for the sake of argument let's just assume everyone we're interested in playing games with is playing in good faith). Bob wants to run a game about dark fantasy angst, and Alice wants to play out <i>Underworld</i>. It's less that the game is wrong, and more that the group wants different things. But people are people, and it's hard to admit to friends that, hey, maybe we shouldn't be doing this together. People bottle that anger or resentment up, and they make the symbol (Trenchcoat McNinja and personal horror, respectively) the object of their anger rather than the person they're actually mad it. This is a bit reductive, but I think you get what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> (Some people will tell you that it <i>is </i>inherently wrong to play campy <i>Blade </i>expies, and go out of your way to inform you of that, but those people are joyless fucks who aren't worth your time.)<br /> <br /> There's also -- and this is not a judgment on you -- a stereotype that any form of power fantasy is a bit juvenile, and that therefore it's a bad thing. Adults aren't allowed to indulge in their ids, and therefore anyone who does is doing it wrong or is childish.<br /> <br /> And you know what? Screw the haters. Play the character with five dots of Blowshitupus. Wear sunglasses at night and wield a katanagun. Be rad.<br /> <br /> <i>Vampire </i>is written with the assumption that participants want to engage in a particular subgenre of gothic fiction. That doesn't mean you have to do it, and as you say, the toolbox is very accommodating. There's lots of room for action and adventure instead of wangst. The thing is -- and again I don't want you to feel judged -- is that it isn't necessary for you to announce your preference for this style of gaming in every post you make. It would be a bit like if I went into every <i>Masquerade </i>thread and started off with &quot;Well I prefer Requiem! But to each their own!&quot; in every post I made. It would be a bit tiresome.<br /> <br /> Real talk: We know, dude. You don't need to apologize for what you like, but you don't need to make the conversation about it every time you talk about <i>Vampire</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 08-15-2017, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T19:06:38-07:00","id":1129559,"title":"","content":"Somewhat off-topic, but what &quot;setting differences&quot; are you opposed to in 2e? I can't even think of a change other than getting rid of the Fog of Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T19:30:13-07:00","id":1129568,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a>, your dislike of personal horror and preference for 1st edition, the reasons for this preference, and your excising of the barely-mentioned emotional deadness from 1st edition requiem are all well known by the forum community at this point. Reiterating it only serves to incite other people to argue the same points. You've seen this happen time and time again. You've been warned that this posting behavior borders on violating rule 2 by inciting others to break the rules. And while your approach to the subject has gotten gradually less dismissive of others' viewpoints, it's hard to view your continued insistence on reiterating the same points as anything but flame baiting or attention seeking. Because you've been largely respectful of others' preferences in the way you keep bringing this subject up, I'm going to give you the benefit of the doubt here, but you are very nearly out of leeway here. From now on, assume that everyone is aware of your preferences regarding Vampire games, and explain them only when asked to do so. Unsolicited explanations of why you don't like personal horror, or the strix, or the defunct line about emotional deadness in vampires in 1st edition requiem, or the minor mechanical and setting changes to 2nd edition requiem, will be considered flame bait.<br /> <br /> I'm leaving this thread open because a thread for discussing hacks and homebrew in Requiem is a perfectly valid thing to have. Let's keep the discussion to that topic and avoid tangents about your personal preferences regarding Vampire and the reasons for said preferences.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T19:32:51-07:00","id":1129571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1129559#post1129559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhat off-topic, but what &quot;setting differences&quot; are you opposed to in 2e? I can't even think of a change other than getting rid of the Fog of Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, she doesn't likes conditions, tilts or beats none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T19:38:16-07:00","id":1129574,"title":"","content":"Deleted; saw mod's message as it updated when I posted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","user":"Ever Professional","date":". 08-15-2017, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T19:45:29-07:00","id":1129578,"title":"","content":"Anyway, onto actual setting hacks. I like to alter the Bloodline creation rules when it comes to blood potency.<br /> <br /> At level 2 potency if the Kindred is hit with a particulary nasty curse, and over the course of the game they start turning the curse to their advantage, then I let the Kindred found a bloodline; no special disciplines or devotions are created. They get four in-clan disciplines, a bloodline gift (possibly a merit of some sort), and the nasty curse as the bloodline bane.<br /> <br /> At Blood Potency four they can form a bloodline without any extra nasty bane; however their bloodline advantage will be learnable by Kindred outside the Bloodline, so there is added risk.<br /> <br /> At blood potency six, when the Kindred has become a true terror of the night, things become interesting. They can create blood sorceries, new disciplines, powerful devotions, and the like; their advantages will not be learnable outside the Bloodline.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's my Bloodline alteration. I'm currently working on some homebrew blood sorceries from some Covenants I was designing, so I might post those sometime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T19:57:01-07:00","id":1129587,"title":"","content":"While scarcely a hack, I vastly prefer the &quot;Tier 1&quot; approach presented in Danse Macabre; no groups larger than coteries, no grand histories or mythologies, just the alien hunger in your gut, the questions in your head, the dying man on the ground in front of you, and the sense that things weren't suppose to go this wrong. Cut away the political distractions, the philosophical questions, and leave nothing but the meat of the predator that was an average Joe yesterday. You ask me for what Vampire should feel like and I say Hotline Miami.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T20:44:06-07:00","id":1129625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1129587#post1129587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While scarcely a hack, I vastly prefer the &quot;Tier 1&quot; approach presented in Danse Macabre; no groups larger than coteries, no grand histories or mythologies, just the alien hunger in your gut, the questions in your head, the dying man on the ground in front of you, and the sense that things weren't suppose to go this wrong. Cut away the political distractions, the philosophical questions, and leave nothing but the meat of the predator that was an average Joe yesterday. You ask me for what Vampire should feel like and I say Hotline Miami.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tier one games are a lot of fun. I love night-to-night survival and interpersonal drama, which tier one is great for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T20:52:55-07:00","id":1129634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1129571#post1129571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, she doesn't likes conditions, tilts or beats none.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of those are setting changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:47:21-07:00","id":1129688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1129574#post1129574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deleted; saw mod's message as it updated when I posted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are of course welcome to leave this post edited if you like, but there was nothing wrong with the original version. My red text was addressed specifically to Camilla because they've displayed a consistent pattern of bringing up these same specific points about what they don't like about Requiem in every couple of posts, and have been asked multiple times not to because it invites edition warring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T23:15:03-07:00","id":1129699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1129688#post1129688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are of course welcome to leave this post edited if you like, but there was nothing wrong with the original version. My red text was addressed specifically to Camilla because they've displayed a consistent pattern of bringing up these same specific points about what they don't like about Requiem in every couple of posts, and have been asked multiple times not to because it invites edition warring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I try to avoid starting (or continuing) stuff that might bring up bad blood, so I'll probably keep it as is for now. Thanks for telling me though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T16:26:46-07:00","id":1130031,"title":"","content":"I didn't get to try it, yet, but I am quite fond of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/997197-blood-is-everything-houserule-set\">this</a> writeup nonetheless. More monstrousness, more focus on what being a monster entails.<br /> <br /> <br /> To make Vampires more heroic is less simply a matter of motivation and actions, in my opinion. Keep the monstrosity in, though, to add drama, tragedy, and give an additional layer to the characters.<br /> You will, invariably, end up with some sort of Anti-Hero, of course. Less hacks, more plothooks:<br /> <br /> The 'Friendly Neighbourhood Vampires' try to atone for the lives they've taken by patroling the area and stopping any crime they meet. Of course, this news will spread, and attract people that emulate them, fans that want to see them. How will they feel when the first imitators die in trying to be like their heroes? What will go through their mind when their fans get endangered, not by some thug, but by a member of the coterie frenzying?<br /> <br /> The Coterie feed exclusively on drug dealers, human traffickers and murderers - this way, they can keep telling themselves that they aren't bad people, that they are in control, that what they are doing is right - that they are not monsters. How long will they be able to keep the illusion alive?<br /> <br /> You could encourage this kind of behavious by giving them a bonus to feeding rolls when NOT drinking from the innocent, or a bonus to their Humanity safe roll, or a bonus to frenzy checks.<br /> <br /> You could make something like a True Love bond mechanic: drinking from your true love causes them ecstasy, and restores willpower. In addition, this blood is much richer in power - you need less blood, thus can feed more often on them. In return, however, , feeding from anyone else means you cause them incredible pain, AND you need more blood than usual: every feeding is fatal.<br /> Furthermore, your true love shares extreme emotions you experience, can always tell where you are, and spending a instant action, can see through your eyes. How will they react when their lover starts feeling joy upon killing evil-doers, how will they react when they experience just what it means to be, feel and think inhumanely? What will they do when frenzy takes them, too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T19:37:26-07:00","id":1130090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1130031#post1130031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The 'Friendly Neighbourhood Vampires' try to atone for the lives they've taken by patroling the area and stopping any crime they meet. Of course, this news will spread, and attract people that emulate them, fans that want to see them. How will they feel when the first imitators die in trying to be like their heroes? What will go through their mind when their fans get endangered, not by some thug, but by a member of the coterie frenzying?<br /> <br /> The Coterie feed exclusively on drug dealers, human traffickers and murderers - this way, they can keep telling themselves that they aren't bad people, that they are in control, that what they are doing is right - that they are not monsters. How long will they be able to keep the illusion alive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically this is encouraged by the Lacea et Sanctum, whom the OP deems villainous, on the basis of being literal wolves to the Lord's sheep.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T11:54:18-07:00","id":1132731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1130031#post1130031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't get to try it, yet, but I am quite fond of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/997197-blood-is-everything-houserule-set\">this</a> writeup nonetheless. More monstrousness, more focus on what being a monster entails.<br /> <br /> <br /> To make Vampires more heroic is less simply a matter of motivation and actions, in my opinion. Keep the monstrosity in, though, to add drama, tragedy, and give an additional layer to the characters.<br /> You will, invariably, end up with some sort of Anti-Hero, of course.<br /> <br /> &lt;snippity&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very interesting set of hacks you reference there, and I'd love to hear if anyone has actually tried them or developed their thinking further in the ~1 year since posting. It's... rather extreme to me as hacks go and the OP references a desire to discuss hacks that veer toward the heroic side.<br /> <br /> Ok. First of all, as others reference, drinking blood and flinging around powers drawn from base human impulses of domination, slavery and rape do not make for heroic characters. That can make for anti-heroes, however, and most players I think would rather view their own characters as anti-heroes within their own story. I'll just leave that assertion on the table, I've neither known a player pleased to run an unjustified moral evil for long, nor would I want to rub shoulders with one. <br /> <br /> Key word here is &quot;unjustified&quot;: vampires are excellent liars, especially to themselves, so their play is in part a matter of exploring to what extent they are willing to lie to themselves (let alone others) as they dance down the primrose path of utilitarianism before looking up at the ruins of all they care for and love. In other words &quot;how many corners do you cut to be the hero of your own story?&quot; Choosing on your first night to feed instead of walking into the sun is the first step on that path, of turning people into objects and paving your road with them.<br /> <br /> To me, then, the first &quot;hack&quot; to Vampire is figuring out for the campaign and the characters what is going on that makes them heroes--or is it really a matter of &quot;survive one more night in a world gone (personally, supernaturally) mad?&quot; That kind of Tier 1 experience is great and can make for a tight story, or blossom into another style once the characters get a handle on themselves. The converse: Blade superheroes and even less introspective trenchcoat ninja monster-of-the-week action imply that the characters have (long ago) worked past their moral, supernatural lifestyle issues and decided dealing with the external monster is sufficient to justify their existence. If your table goes for that, then cool.<br /> <br /> So what does &quot;setting hacks&quot; mean, then? Things that help shove aside the moral introspection built into the system? Things that veer the story toward teen angst and sparkles? Supermen with fangs? Marvel Anti-Heroic Role-Playing? <br /> <br /> Anyway, here is reference to one suggestion on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1113501-daywalking/page2\">daywalking</a> with a contribution inside it. The the net effect is to enable vampires to wander about during the day to one degree or another, which significantly changes many of the trope dynamics and can make them more like Superman-by-night/Kent-by-day if you like. I'm intending to try it a bit and see what happens. Otherwise, consider that so long as the players/characters can point to a bigger and meaner bad than them, they can justify or handwave around the morally reprehensible parts of kindred existence long enough to come up with a &quot;fix&quot; of some sort. That's pretty much the whole point of the Ordo Dracul, unless you're into knowledge-for-knowledge sake.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T12:09:29-07:00","id":1132739,"title":"","content":"For vampires to be heroic you basically need to take away all the elements of vampirism that make it a curse. Heroes, as they were first conceived by romanticism are infallible. Which turns them into Mary Sues. Which is why you get such a negative connotation out of this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T12:16:13-07:00","id":1132742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1132739#post1132739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For vampires to be heroic you basically need to take away all the elements of vampirism that make it a curse. Heroes, as they were first conceived by romanticism are infallible. Which turns them into Mary Sues. Which is why you get such a negative connotation out of this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I politely disagree. To answer your statement, I must clarify that the curse is still there in my games (I don't do daywalking vampires, for example), but it is downplayed and can be overcome if one tries hard enough (for example, a Vampire can achieve Golconda and become human again). So I guess my vampires are more anti-heroes than pure straight-up heroes. But they aren't inherently villainous either.<br /> <br /> Basically, my goal was to turn Vampire from a game of damnation and personal horror into a game of redemption and salvation, if that is what you are asking.<br /> <br /> Again, I don't want to beat a dead horse like before, but I'm getting the impression you may be somewhat confused with the intent of my Vampire games, so I thought I'd clarify. By this point, I've made it perfectly clear that my Vampire games are essentially redemption stories and I won't discuss it any further unless asked about it first.<br /> <br /> Let's just stick to discussing setting hacks for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 08-22-2017, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:00:17-07:00","id":1132756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1132742#post1132742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I politely disagree. To answer your statement, I must clarify that the curse is still there in my games (I don't do daywalking vampires, for example), but it is downplayed and can be overcome if one tries hard enough (for example, a Vampire can achieve Golconda and become human again). So I guess my vampires are more anti-heroes than pure straight-up heroes. But they aren't inherently villainous either.<br /> <br /> Basically, my goal was to turn Vampire from a game of damnation and personal horror into a game of redemption and salvation, if that is what you are asking.<br /> <br /> Again, I don't want to beat a dead horse like before, but I'm getting the impression you may be somewhat confused with the intent of my Vampire games, so I thought I'd clarify. By this point, I've made it perfectly clear that my Vampire games are essentially redemption stories and I won't discuss it any further unless asked about it first.<br /> <br /> Let's just stick to discussing setting hacks for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>A story about achieving Golconda, with all of the inherent difficulties about doing such is a great basis for a chronicle, don't get me wrong, and you could likely follow with the struggles that is maintaining such an exalted state. How easy is to achieve such enlightenment in your setting? How do you go about it? What are the benefits and drawbacks of the vampiric nirvana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:11:37-07:00","id":1132762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1132756#post1132756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A story about achieving Golconda, with all of the inherent difficulties about doing such is a great basis for a chronicle, don't get me wrong, and you could likely follow with the struggles that is maintaining such an exalted state. How easy is to achieve such enlightenment in your setting? How do you go about it? What are the benefits and drawbacks of the vampiric nirvana?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically, when a Vampire achieves Golconda, they become human again and are no longer a vampire and are eternally free from the curse of vampirism, essentially immune to the Embrace upon achieving Golconda.<br /> <br /> It is a difficult state to achieve, and I've yet to have a chronicle last long enough for me to actually plan out the process to become human once more. I need to think on this, because you are correct that a redemption chronicle would be interesting to explore in-depth. But the idea I had for my redemption chronicles is that the game I design is meant to distract you from seeking Golconda via the politics between covenants and all the action-adventure stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:53:23-07:00","id":1132789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1132739#post1132739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For vampires to be heroic you basically need to take away all the elements of vampirism that make it a curse. Heroes, as they were first conceived by romanticism are infallible. Which turns them into Mary Sues. Which is why you get such a negative connotation out of this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go further back, though, and you end up with tragic, curse-plagued and disaster-stricken heroes like Heracles or (more recent, maybe) Siegfried. Those would work well with a vampire looking to redeem himself, no?<br /> Or take modern human superheroes: Batman is basically a deeply-traumatized boy throwing a tantrum and enacting his own therapy by punishing people by proxi, Tony Stark is arrogant, vaine and an addict incapable of forming and keeping bonds, a realistic Steve Rogers would most likely have tons of problems adjusting to a bunch of changes due to having out-of-touch values, and Peter Parker has an enormous guilt-complex.<br /> Highlighting these qualities is enough to make them usable concepts, I think.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a> You want a Hero story? Fine, easy enough. But don't go superhero - go for a more personal route. You wan't something that jives with Golconda? Okay, how about this: Go full on Campbell's Monomyth. Take a look at the Hero's Journey:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hhk4N9A0oCA\" data-code=\"Hhk4N9A0oCA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Hhk4N9A0oCA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> Don't adhvere slavishly to it. But use this as a kind of blueprint.<br /> My take on this, with what little I know, would be: Start with your human characters, Call them to Adventure via the Embrace. Have them delve into Vampire Society, an exhilarating and promising, if scary experience, then the corners and edges of their new unlife show more and more and start wearing on them. They are not able to lie to themselves about the fact that this is a curse, that bad things can and will happen if this keeps one. Make them <b>want </b>to search out Golconda. How do they achieve it? How about not by doing great things, save lifes, but by acts of compassion, of courage, of humbleness, generosity, wisdom and honour: essentially striving for the best of humanity, not for heroics - take a note from Disney's Hercules if you want to. Want some heroic deeds? Go make them reduce Kindred influence on society, challenge those that prevent access to the knowledge of Golconda, rip out the parasite that is Kindred society wholly if you want to. But make sure that caring for that one victim, with warmth, with love, that ignoring their own goals for the benefit of that homeless guy is what brings them forwards. I'm sure you can fluff it up any way you want to.<br /> The important thing is: When they achieve it, they will have overcome their own monstrous nature and become <i>better </i>human beings. What higher mark of a hero than to overcome the darkness inside?<br /> <br /> And, to be honest, a powerful curse only makes the fight harder, and the victory that much sweeter in this case. But that's just my personal preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:55:02-07:00","id":1132790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1132789#post1132789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Go further back, though, and you end up with tragic, curse-plagued and disaster-stricken heroes like Heracles or (more recent, maybe) Siegfried. Those would work well with a vampire looking to redeem himself, no?<br /> Or take modern human superheroes: Batman is basically a deeply-traumatized boy throwing a tantrum and enacting his own therapy by punishing people by proxi, Tony Stark is arrogant, vaine and an addict incapable of forming and keeping bonds, a realistic Steve Rogers would most likely have tons of problems adjusting to a bunch of changes due to having out-of-touch values, and Peter Parker has an enormous guilt-complex.<br /> Highlighting these qualities is enough to make them usable concepts, I think.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a> You want a Hero story? Fine, easy enough. But don't go superhero - go for a more personal route. You wan't something that jives with Golconda? Okay, how about this: Go full on Campbell's Monomyth. Take a look at the Hero's Journey:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hhk4N9A0oCA\" data-code=\"Hhk4N9A0oCA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Hhk4N9A0oCA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> Don't adhvere slavishly to it. But use this as a kind of blueprint.<br /> My take on this, with what little I know, would be: Start with your human characters, Call them to Adventure via the Embrace. Have them delve into Vampire Society, an exhilarating and promising, if scary experience, then the corners and edges of their new unlife show more and more and start wearing on them. They are not able to lie to themselves about the fact that this is a curse, that bad things can and will happen if this keeps one. Make them <b>want </b>to search out Golconda. How do they achieve it? How about not by doing great things, save lifes, but by acts of compassion, of courage, of humbleness, generosity, wisdom and honour: essentially striving for the best of humanity, not for heroics - take a note from Disney's Hercules if you want to. Want some heroic deeds? Go make them reduce Kindred influence on society, challenge those that prevent access to the knowledge of Golconda, rip out the parasite that is Kindred society wholly if you want to. But make sure that caring for that one victim, with warmth, with love, that ignoring their own goals for the benefit of that homeless guy is what brings them forwards. I'm sure you can fluff it up any way you want to.<br /> The important thing is: When they achieve it, they will have overcome their own monstrous nature and become <i>better </i>human beings. What higher mark of a hero than to overcome the darkness inside?<br /> <br /> And, to be honest, a powerful curse only makes the fight harder, and the victory that much sweeter in this case. But that's just my personal preference.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this approach, actually. I honestly do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T16:53:49-07:00","id":1132842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1132789#post1132789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Go further back, though, and you end up with tragic, curse-plagued and disaster-stricken heroes like Heracles or (more recent, maybe) Siegfried. Those would work well with a vampire looking to redeem himself, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in the earlier tragedies, the hero is never to blame for them, there's always someone who orchestrates the disasters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-23-2017, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T18:09:30-07:00","id":1132872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1129520-heroic-vampires-and-other-setting-hacks-setting-hack-homebrew-general-discussion?p=1132842#post1132842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even in the earlier tragedies, it's the hero is never to blame for them, there's always someone who orchestrates the disasters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to disagree at first, but you are absolutely right. It's my current reading that makes many of them self-entitled assholes (Beowulf anyone?). Sorry!<br /> <br /> At least we still got the flawed modern (anti)heroes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}